  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Open-Source initiative is targeted explicitly at investees who benefit from the investment of public money, and in this, participation is a requirement of investment. 

Additionally, the Open-Source initiative would be open to the participation of any developer or market player who would be prepared to ascribe to the principles, even without funding from an Alliance partner.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The performance targets include:

1) Initiate the Open-Source initiative.
2) Pilot the data collection process.
3) Assemble, analyze and develop outputs from the pilot data.
4) Disseminate pilot outputs.
5) Institutionalize the Open-Source initiative.
6) Bespoke data collection process
7) Assemble, analyze and develop outputs from the pilot data.
8) Disseminate outputs.
9) Service the AHIA
10) Undertake AHIA-sponsored research.</narrative>
  </description>
